{"id":"30664297001","kind":"article","title":"反对合理化","author":"Rob Bensinger","original_authors":["Rob Bensinger"],"original_source_urls":["https://www.readthesequences.com/Against-Rationalization-Sequence"],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"理性 & 克服偏见","date":"2025-03-21","updated":"2026-10-27","votes":19,"comment_count":0,"minutes":2,"chars":726,"keywords":["合理化","动机性推理","判断偏差"],"summary":"作者借达特茅斯—普林斯顿比赛提醒：人们常在事后编造理由，使既有观点显得连贯，却不一定提高判断准确性；正文随后列出相关的反合理化文章系列。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/30664297001","restoration":null,"toc":[],"html":"<p data-pid=\"5l61iHy_\">这场达特茅斯-普林斯顿的比赛给我们带来一个启示：我们的大部分推理过程实际上是在事后合理化——我们编造故事，让自己当前的观点显得更加连贯和有道理，但这并不一定能提高观点的准确性。<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://www.readthesequences.com/Against-Rationalization-Sequence\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《反对合理化》</a>系列探讨了这一问题，而<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://www.readthesequences.com/Against-Doublethink-Sequence\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《对抗双重思想》</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>（关于自我欺骗）和<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://www.readthesequences.com/Seeing-With-Fresh-Eyes-Sequence\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《用新眼光看问题》</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>（关于挑战我们识别与预期和假设不符的证据的能力）系列则对此进行了进一步阐述。</p><p data-pid=\"jraV0Azu\">——<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://www.readthesequences.com/Rationality-An-Introduction\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《理性：序言》</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup>by Rob Bensinger</p><hr/><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-image=\"https://pic1.zhimg.com/v2-873ecdcd65dde2e1f16891677abf0be2_qhd.jpg\" data-image-height=\"3648\" data-image-width=\"5472\" data-tm-id=\"8246788669\" href=\"#/post/8246788669\">Thoughts Memo：了解偏见可能反而有害</a><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-image=\"https://pica.zhimg.com/v2-f16154e462cbc26c412d0d86572ddec0_qhd.jpg\" data-image-height=\"4160\" data-image-width=\"6240\" data-tm-id=\"12593770040\" href=\"#/post/12593770040\">Thoughts Memo：逐步自我更新</a><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-image=\"https://pic1.zhimg.com/v2-d70588c5cecd27bd0a7fdb0eb62dcce0_l.jpg\" data-image-height=\"1024\" data-image-width=\"1024\" data-tm-id=\"12852320444\" href=\"#/post/12852320444\">Thoughts Memo：以一当千的论证谬误</a><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-image=\"https://pic2.zhimg.com/v2-1efa9d935aef83dce2e8e809a4a0e989_qhd.jpg\" data-image-height=\"4000\" data-image-width=\"6000\" data-tm-id=\"13265385885\" href=\"#/post/13265385885\">Thoughts Memo：结论从何而来</a><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-image=\"https://pic1.zhimg.com/v2-db1516149e617d9ff143a15423233b22_qhd.jpg\" data-image-height=\"4000\" data-image-width=\"6000\" data-tm-id=\"15300705897\" href=\"#/post/15300705897\">Thoughts Memo：什么是证据筛选？</a><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-image=\"https://pic2.zhimg.com/v2-49a182753963b1fad90ba797b5032b39_qhd.jpg\" data-image-height=\"1375\" data-image-width=\"2000\" data-tm-id=\"15807962622\" href=\"#/post/15807962622\">Thoughts Memo：合理化</a><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-image=\"https://picx.zhimg.com/v2-dcd915edb68d9b76f8b25b8f5a2f57b9_qhd.jpg\" data-image-height=\"2832\" data-image-width=\"4256\" data-tm-id=\"19114455919\" href=\"#/post/19114455919\">Thoughts Memo：理性的论证</a><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-image=\"https://pic1.zhimg.com/v2-02b09c3cb588f3973c748671f5f2fca0_qhd.jpg\" data-image-height=\"1944\" data-image-width=\"2592\" data-tm-id=\"23207691441\" href=\"#/post/23207691441\">Thoughts Memo：规避你信念中的真正弱点</a><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-image=\"https://pic4.zhimg.com/v2-fbdb4d24d7e23ed91e29ade9c9c8e8db_qhd.jpg\" data-image-height=\"3353\" data-image-width=\"5961\" data-tm-id=\"25143636684\" href=\"#/post/25143636684\">Thoughts Memo：动机性停止和动机性继续</a><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-image=\"https://pic2.zhimg.com/v2-7ed6856317a56dd90d9c1db0163deef5_qhd.jpg\" data-image-height=\"3456\" d